[polypile zaps destroy items in current code - list gets shorter]

I think you're not seeing what you think you are; if you've played with
big stacks of stuff, you'll notice that nethack _consolidates_ like
items; probably your polypile list shortens every time two different
things polymorph into (the combined number of instances of) the same
thing. Of course, this only works for things like arrows, daggers, gems,
and so on that are listed with a count and an item name, rather than
just separately.

When I was abusing the game another way (a few 100K turns at an altar),
I piled the junk mislaid by unfortunately deceased wandering monsters in
an upstairs room, sorted out by "blessed, cursed, normal" and by item
class; (it was a _big_ room), into piles hundreds of items deep, and saw
this consolidation happening.

In other words, you still have as many _things_, just fewer _kinds_ of
counted things and thus fewer entries in the list.

I think.

